.TH BIGFLOATRECIPROCAL 3 "2026-09-21" "BigNums" "Library Functions Manual"
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
bigFloatReciprocal, bigFloatDiv, bigFloatSqrt \- compute a reciprocal, quotient, or square root
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqbignums.h\(dq
.sp
.BI "int bigFloatReciprocal(BigFloat *" "result" ","
.BI "    const BigFloat *" "x" ", int " "target_limbs" ");"
.sp
.BI "int bigFloatDiv(BigFloat *" "result" ", const BigFloat *" "a" ","
.BI "    const BigFloat *" "b" ", int " "target_limbs" ");"
.sp
.BI "int bigFloatSqrt(BigFloat *" "result" ", const BigFloat *" "x" ","
.BI "    int " "target_limbs" ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bigFloatReciprocal()
computes 1/x using Newton iteration y = y * (2 \- x*y).
.B bigFloatDiv()
computes the reciprocal of b and multiplies it by a.
.B bigFloatSqrt()
computes the nonnegative square root of x by iterating y = (y + x/y) / 2.
Use a distinct result object and initialized inputs.
.PP
Reciprocal and square root clamp target_limbs to 1 through MAX_LIMBS.
They use min(target_limbs + 2, MAX_LIMBS) to choose the iteration count,
then truncate the final result to target_limbs.
Division limits the reciprocal only; its final product is not truncated.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Reciprocal returns 0 on success or INT_MAX for zero input or a delegated
arithmetic failure.  Division propagates reciprocal or multiplication status.
Square root returns \-1 for a negative sign, including signed zero, or a
failed inner division/addition.  Positive zero succeeds.  Final normalization
can return INT_MAX; otherwise the return value is 0.
Do not consume the output after an error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
BigFloat two, root;
bigFloatFromUint32(&two, 2);
if (bigFloatSqrt(&root, &two, 4) != 0)
    return 1;
printBigFloat(&root, 6);
.EE
.SH BUGS
Target limb count limits storage, not guaranteed correct bits.
Intermediate results are not truncated to a guard-limb budget and may overflow
before final truncation.  Square root requests MAX_LIMBS precision for each
inner division.  Exponent calculations are not all checked for overflow.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bigFloatTruncate (3),
.BR bigFloatMul (3),
.BR printBigFloat (3),
.BR bignums (3),
.BR bignums (7)
